'''Melitto''' were a [[species]] of [[Insectoid|insectile]] [[humanoid]]s native to the [[planet]] [[Li-Toran]]. They had no [[eye]]s or [[mouth]], but were capable of sensing their environment using super-sensitive [[Cilium|cilia]]. Melitto had [[chitin]] plates on their heads and [[Limb|forearms]], and required the use of [[Cybernetics|cybernetic]] [[breathing tube]]s when operating in [[alien]] [[atmosphere]]s.

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:CaM_front_character_art.png|thumb|left|The Melittos' faces were covered in chitinous plates.]]
With a body comprising a head, a torso, two [[Limb|legs]], two arms, and five-fingered hands, the Melitto were [[humanoid]]s.<ref name="TFA VD" /> Nevertheless, the segmented plates of [[chitin]] visible on their heads and [[hair]]y forearms betrayed their [[Insectoid|insectile]] nature. The Melitto face was covered in four plates, the largest being at the top, but did not feature visible [[eye]]s or [[mouth]].<ref name="The Weapon of a Jedi" /> Melittos were blind and relied heavily on other senses. On [[Kijimi]], the [[Ashiga Clan]]'s architecture was embedded with metal on the ground to feel where they were going.<ref name="Outlaws BTS">{{UbisoftYouTube|BxyqrPk51KM|Star Wars Outlaws: Behind The Scenes &ndash; Navigating the Underworld}}</ref> They are also able to detect lies thanks to their receptors.<ref name="SWO" />

However, they did have auditory organs,<ref name="AotG" /> and the small bristles lining their body<ref name="Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> were specialized, feathery [[Cilium|cilia]] that could sense vibrations and detect electrical fields. Additionally, those cilia gave the Melitto a keen sense of smell. Their extraordinary scent-memories helped them navigate just as well as if they had eyes and gave them extensive identification and tracking skills.<ref name="AotG" />

When operating in [[atmosphere]]s different from their own, the Melitto wore [[Cybernetics|breathing tubes]] and carried dispensers filled with [[sugar]]y nutrient fluid.<ref name="AotG" />

The species had at least two [[Gender|sexes]]: male and female.<ref name="AotG" /> One known individual, a male named [[Sarco Plank]], stood 1.82 [[meter]]s tall.<ref name="DB">{{Databank|sarco-plank|Sarco Plank}}</ref> The Melitto language consisted of humming sounds produced by their facial plates. To communicate with other species, they wore [[Vocabulator|vocoders]] that translated their hums into an understandable voice.<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" />

==Society and culture==
{{Quote|So ND, this uh, Hive thing. How does it work?"<br />"It's the foundation of Melitto culture. Everyone obeys the Queen and puts the clan's needs over their own.|Kay Vess and ND-5|<ref name="SWO">''[[Star Wars Outlaws]]''</ref>}}
Melitto were eusocial beings who lived in [[Melitto hive|hives]] ruled by [[queen]]s and their adolescent female servants&mdash;called [[Myrmitrix|myrmitrices]]&mdash;who in turn controlled their own stables of male workers&mdash;or [[myrmite]]s&mdash;who gathered [[Foodstuff|food]], built the physical hive structure, and battled other hives as [[soldier-myrmite]]s. Whenever a hive's population increased too much for it to operate at full efficiency, it became necessary to found a new hive. The myrmitrices then started fighting each other with the help of their warrior followers. When a victor emerged, she gained the right to be queen of a new hive. The myrmites who had the misfortune of surviving their myrmitrix's defeat were cast away from their hive, becoming [[ronin]]. Most ronin left their [[homeworld]] to become expert [[Hunting|hunters]] and [[Thief|thieves]]. Some, however, were rumored to found their own queenless communities in the subterranean caves of their planet,<ref name="Pointed Questions">{{FantasyFlightGames|url=en/news/2017/9/18/pointed-questions|text=Pointed Questions}}</ref> such as the [[Hive Ronin]].<ref name="Cyphars and Masks">''[[Cyphers and Masks]]''</ref> Some some of these hives turned to organized crime as a means to ensure the survival of the same, such as the [[Ashiga Clan]].<ref name="SWO" />

==History==
[[File:Melitto-CaM.png|thumb|right|220px|A Melitto spy]]
The Melitto evolved on [[Li-Toran]], a dismal and storm-buffeted [[planet]] situated in the [[Inner Rim Territories|Inner Rim]] region of [[the galaxy]].<ref name="AotG" />

==Melitto in the galaxy==
In addition to their homeworld, the Melitto also developed a presence on several neighboring planets. However, due to the nature of their society, the Melitto rarely ventured in the wider galaxy, and those who did were mostly ronin. Thanks to their scent-memories, the Melitto made excellent [[doctor]]s, capable of detecting chemical components that were markers for diseases.<ref name="AotG" /> The Ashiga Clan was a criminal syndicate<ref name="Outlaws">''[[Star Wars Outlaws]]''</ref> built around a hierarchical Melitto hive.<ref name="OutlawsSetting">{{WebCite|url=https://www.gameinformer.com/exclusive-interview/2023/08/15/star-wars-outlaws-setting-is-a-dream-playground-according-to|text=Star Wars Outlaws' Setting Is A Dream Playground, According To Narrative Director|work=Game Informer|author=Kyle Hillard|date=2023-08-15|access-date=2023-08-30|archivedate=20230827125620}}</ref> The Clan had been active since the days of the [[High Republic Era]] and survived into the [[Imperial Era]]. During the [[Galactic Civil War]], the [[Ashiga Clan]] was led by [[Ashiga|Queen Ashiga]]. The queen's daughter, [[Krisk Ashiga]], did not agree with the way her mother ruled, mainly due to her agreement with the [[Galactic Empire]], which led her to plot to dethrone her and become the new queen.<ref name="Outlaws" />

One known Melitto ronin was [[Sarco Plank]], who worked as a [[bounty hunter]], jungle guide, and tomb raider on [[Devaron]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]]. There, Plank notably [[Skirmish in the Temple of Eedit|dueled]] the [[Padawan|trainee]] [[Jedi]] [[Luke Skywalker]] among the ruins of the [[Temple of Eedit]].<ref name="The Weapon of a Jedi" /> The encounter left Plank with a near-fatal [[lightsaber]] wound. More than three [[Standard decade|decades]] later, the ronin had found his way to [[Niima Outpost]] on [[Jakku]], where he operated as a [[scavenger]] and bounty hunter.<ref name="DB" />

